{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2104","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2104","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2104\",\"parent_revision\":\"05cf458608a678a0350b401f863f389247a0b585\",\"root_revision\":\"e7e65d69fba3e191a1e69f471d60adf1dd67d867d1020b74e7acbae6a543795d\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **run /complete-implementation quality gates in an isolated worktree** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/no-mistakes.md \u2014 pattern: Isolated Validation Worktree (Patterns Worth Adopting / Non-Blocking Isolated Worktree)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-03\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-04)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n\\n| Input | Condition | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Protect developer working tree from auto-fix mutations during quality gate run |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | SKILL.md change to `complete-implementation`; worktree lifecycle steps; approval gate |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | `git worktree add/remove`, `prepare_clean_worktree.sh`, SAM MCP, `artifact_list`/`artifact_read` |\\n| Constraints | DERIVABLE | Worktree path pattern from item; ULID generation method not pinned (any codebase ULID tool satisfies) |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | `prepare_clean_worktree.sh` handles dirty working tree; `work-milestone` shows established worktree pattern |\\n| Verification expectations | AVAILABLE | Measurable signal fully specified in item |\\n\\n**Gap**: ULID generation method not specified. `no-mistakes` (research source) uses `oklog/ulid`; this codebase's script layer uses Python \u2014 `uuid` or a Python ULID library would satisfy. Not a planning blocker.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Developer safety feature. Auto-fix mutations (T1 fix loop, T5 doc regeneration) currently land directly in the developer's working tree without consent. Developers cannot safely run `/complete-implementation` on a branch with uncommitted WIP. The `work-milestone` skill already solved this for milestone-scoped work; parity for single-feature quality gates is the natural extension. No blocking dependencies.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Any developer who has uncommitted WIP when running `/complete-implementation` \u2014 current behavior silently mutates their working tree via T1 fix loop (SKILL.md lines 612\u2013618) and T5 doc regeneration\\n- Bottleneck: Without isolation, `/complete-implementation` is unsafe to run on branches with unstaged changes, reducing usability to clean-tree-only workflows\\n- Affected files: `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` (primary); no other skills require changes\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Developers can invoke `/complete-implementation` with WIP in their working tree and have it remain untouched\\n- Auto-fix commits from T1 and T5 become reviewable diffs on a separate branch before landing on the feature branch\\n- Establishes worktree isolation as the consistent pattern across all quality gate scenarios (single-feature and milestone)\\n- Developer approval/rejection gate gives explicit consent control over quality gate auto-fixes\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `/complete-implementation` is invoked:\\n\\n1. A git worktree is created at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/qg-worktrees/{branch}-{ulid}` before any phase dispatches\\n2. All 6 quality gate phases (T1\u2013T6) execute with their working directory set to this worktree\\n3. Auto-fix commits from T1's fix loop and T5's documentation regeneration land on the worktree branch, not the developer's feature branch\\n4. The developer's original working tree (including any uncommitted changes) is never read, written, or staged by quality gate execution\\n5. After all phases complete, the developer sees a diff of what quality gates changed and approves or rejects before the worktree branch is fast-forwarded onto their feature branch\\n6. On completion (success or rejection), the worktree directory is removed\\n7. `git status` in the original working tree reflects the same state as before `/complete-implementation` was invoked\\n\\nPlan artifacts (feature-context, architect, T0-baseline, etc.) continue to be accessed via `artifact_read` (MCP) from within the worktree \u2014 the artifact manifest system already handles this (line 354 of current SKILL.md).\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe `/complete-implementation` SKILL.md gains a new section \\\"Worktree Setup\\\" inserted between \\\"Pre-Phase: Artifact Discovery\\\" and \\\"Quality Gate Plan Creation\\\". This section documents:\\n\\n- The `git worktree add` command creating the QG worktree at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/qg-worktrees/{branch}-{ulid}`\\n- How quality gate agents receive the worktree path as their working directory (passed as a context variable)\\n- The developer approval step after all phases complete: diff preview, fast-forward to feature branch or discard\\n- The `git worktree remove --force` cleanup step (run on success AND on rejection)\\n\\nThe SAM Dispatch Loop section is updated to pass the worktree path to each dispatched QG agent so they set their working directory appropriately.\\n\\nNo new scripts, MCP tools, or agents are required. The existing `prepare_clean_worktree.sh` behavior (stash dirty working tree before worktree creation) carries over without modification.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Running `/complete-implementation #N` against a feature branch with uncommitted changes: after the run, `git status` in the original working tree shows exactly the same uncommitted changes as before (same content, no new staged or unstaged files added by quality gate execution)\\n2. During the run, `ls ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/qg-worktrees/` lists at least one entry matching `{branch}-*`\\n3. After the run completes (success or rejection), `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/qg-worktrees/{branch}-*` has been removed (`git worktree list` no longer shows it)\\n4. The SKILL.md for `complete-implementation` contains a section titled \\\"Worktree Setup\\\" positioned between \\\"Pre-Phase: Artifact Discovery\\\" and \\\"Quality Gate Plan Creation\\\"\\n5. The \\\"Worktree Setup\\\" section documents: the `git worktree add` command with the path pattern, how QG agents are passed the worktree path, the developer approval/rejection gate, and the `git worktree remove` cleanup step\\n6. T1 auto-fix commits and T5 documentation commits appear on the worktree branch and are absent from the developer's feature branch until the developer approves the diff\\n7. If the developer rejects the QG diff at the approval gate, the worktree branch is discarded and `git log` on the developer's feature branch shows no new commits from quality gate execution\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|---|---|\\n| Skill | /dh:complete-implementation |\\n| Skill | /dh:work-milestone |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/scripts/prepare_clean_worktree.sh |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md lines 44, 100\u2013129 \u2014 established `git worktree add` pattern for kage-bunshin sessions |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md lines 346\u2013357 \u2014 artifact manifest system for worktree-isolated agents (`artifact_read` via MCP) |\\n| Research | research/developer-tools/no-mistakes.md \u2014 Non-Blocking Isolated Worktree pattern (source of this item) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 `prepare_clean_worktree.sh` and the `artifact_read` MCP tool (the two required infrastructure pieces) already exist and are proven\\n- Blocks: None identified\\n- Related: #1723 (`artifact_read` token ceiling) \u2014 large artifacts produced by quality gate agents inside the worktree context may hit the 10K-token ceiling, but #1723 does not block this item from being implemented\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone. All required infrastructure exists: `git worktree`, `prepare_clean_worktree.sh`, and the artifact manifest system. This item is a SKILL.md edit plus workflow documentation, not a new tool.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 The implementation is a SKILL.md edit to `complete-implementation`. The worktree lifecycle commands are already proven in `work-milestone` (lines 44, 100\u2013129). The artifact discovery path for worktree-isolated agents is already documented and in use (line 354). No new scripts, MCP tools, or agents required. Scope: one new SKILL.md section (~40\u201380 lines) and a targeted update to the SAM Dispatch Loop section to pass the worktree path to QG agents as their working directory.\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nResearch entry: ./research/developer-tools/no-mistakes.md \u2014 Non-Blocking Isolated Worktree pattern.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`/complete-implementation` runs all 6 quality-gate phases (T1 Code Review through T6 Context Refinement) directly against the developer's current working tree. The SKILL.md at `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` only mentions \\\"worktree-isolated agents\\\" once (line 354), referring to plan-artifact discovery via the artifact manifest \u2014 not to running the gates themselves in an isolated worktree. The Quality Gate Plan Creation section (lines 380\u2013438) creates the SAM plan and dispatches agents in-place. There is no `git worktree add` step, no temporary directory creation, and no rollback step that protects the developer's working tree from auto-fix mutations performed by T1's fix loop (lines 612\u2013618) or by T5 documentation regeneration. The `work-milestone` skill DOES use isolated worktrees (line 44, line 124 of `work-milestone/SKILL.md`), but only for parallel kage-bunshin sessions across milestone items \u2014 it is not invoked for single-feature `/complete-implementation` runs.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`/complete-implementation` creates an isolated worktree at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/qg-worktrees/{branch}-{ulid}` before any phase dispatches. All 6 phases execute inside that worktree. Auto-fix commits land on the worktree's branch first. The developer's original working tree is never mutated by quality-gate execution. After completion, the worktree branch is fast-forwarded onto the developer's branch only after the developer approves the diff (or the existing autonomy mode authorizes it). The worktree is destroyed on success or on rejection.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun: `/complete-implementation #N` against a feature branch with uncommitted changes in the working tree. After the run completes, `git status` in the original working tree shows the same uncommitted changes intact (unchanged hash for any unstaged file). Inspect `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/qg-worktrees/` \u2014 directory exists during the run, removed after. New SKILL.md section \\\"Worktree Setup\\\" between \\\"Pre-Phase: Artifact Discovery\\\" and \\\"Quality Gate Plan Creation\\\" documents the worktree lifecycle commands.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4fa6b0761a59843a1b7ade96f7744bcf42c50b3f7fc6758aff832b1a5cf6b4e4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPuhW6g\"}"}